    "fun": "The Minnesota State Capitol in Saint Paul was designed by Cass Gilbert, a young architect from St. Paul. He finished it in 1905. He did such a good job that 30 years later, he was hired to design an even bigger building: the U.S. Supreme Court building in Washington, D.C. Same architect, both buildings, marble and dome and all.",
