    "fun": "The First Amendment packs FIVE rights into one sentence: religion, speech, press, assembly, and petition. Most Americans can name only one or two when asked. And here's the key: these rights belong to EVERYONE living in the U.S. — not just citizens. The Bill of Rights talks about 'the people' and 'persons,' not just 'citizens.'",
