    "fun": "In 1943, during World War II, the Supreme Court ruled that no one in the U.S. can be forced to say the Pledge — even at school. Forcing someone to declare loyalty would violate the First Amendment. So when you say the Pledge, you're choosing to. Real loyalty is freely given, not commanded.",
