    "fun": "New citizens take their Oath of Allegiance at a public ceremony — at a courthouse, or sometimes inside the National Archives in front of the actual Constitution and Bill of Rights. A version of this oath has been said by new Americans since 1790. That's over 235 years of welcoming new citizens to the United States.",
