    "why": "Serving your country doesn't only mean wearing a uniform. The Founders thought a republic couldn't survive unless ordinary citizens did their part: voting, paying taxes, obeying laws, helping their community. Service is what makes the whole system work. In a self-governing country, the citizens ARE the government — so they have to show up.",
    "fun": "The Founders thought a republic couldn't survive unless citizens did their part. They called this 'civic virtue.' Service doesn't only mean joining the military — voting, paying taxes, even just obeying the law are all forms of service. They're what makes self-government actually work. A republic needs citizens who care enough to keep it running.",
