    "fun": "In 1782, an army officer wrote George Washington suggesting he become King of the new country. Washington wrote back instantly, saying he viewed the idea 'with abhorrence' — that no event in the entire war had given him 'more painful sensations.' The man who could have been America's king chose to become its citizen instead.",
