    "why": "'E Pluribus Unum' is Latin for 'Out of many, one.' Originally it meant 13 separate colonies becoming one nation. Today it means something even bigger: people from many countries, languages, religions, and backgrounds becoming one American people. It still appears on most U.S. coins and the Great Seal of the United States — the official symbol of our country.",
